    "title": "How to Watch Padres vs. Tigers: Live Stream or on TV - Bleacher Nation",
    "text": "The San Diego Padres (0-2), led by Fernando Tatis Jr., host Gleyber Torres and the Detroit Tigers (2-0) on Saturday, with first pitch at 8:40 p.m. ET. Keep scrolling to find out all the details on how to watch San Diego take on Detroit live. When is Padres vs. Tigers and when does it start? This game between the Padres and Tigers will take place on Saturday, March 28, 2026. You should expect the opening pitch at 8:40 p.m. ET. Where to watch Padres vs. Tigers The Padres and Tigers will hit the diamond at Petco Park for this matchup on March 28, and if you’d like to see the action live, get your tickets now from Vivid Seats! What channel is the game on? You can catch this game live on Padres.TV and DSN. Padres vs. Tigers Game Preview The Tigers took down the Padres 5-2 yesterday, with Enmanuel De Jesus getting the win (1.0 IP, 0 R, 1 H, 2 K) and Torres leading the way offensively (going 1 for 3). Jeremiah Estrada (0.2 IP, 4 R, 1 H, 2 K) took the loss for the Padres. Padres Stats, Odds & Insights (2025) The Padres were favored on the moneyline 92 total times last season. They finished 55-37 in those games. San Diego hit 152 home runs last season, the third-lowest total in MLB. Last year the Padres ranked 22nd in baseball slugging .390. San Diego’s 3.63 team ERA ranked third among all MLB pitching staffs. Last season Padres pitchers combined for the No. 3 WHIP in baseball (1.209). Tigers Stats, Odds & Insights (2025) The Tigers were underdogs 55 times last season and won 27, or 49.1%, of those games. Detroit ranked 10th in Major League Baseball with 198 home runs. The Tigers ranked 11th in the majors with a .413 team slugging percentage. Detroit pitched to a 3.95 ERA last season, which ranked 15th in baseball. The Tigers had a combined WHIP of 1.250 as a pitching staff, which ranked 13th in MLB. Padres Key Players to Watch (2025 Stats) Randy Vasquez will make his first start of the season for the Padres. When he last appeared on Sunday, Sept. 28, 2025, the 27-year-old righty threw in relief and went one inning against the Arizona Diamondbacks. Tatis finished last season with 25 home runs, 71 RBI and a batting average of .268. Manny Machado finished with a .275 average, 27 home runs and 95 RBI. Ramon Laureano finished last season with 24 home runs, 76 RBI and a batting average of .281. Tigers Key Players (2025 Stats) Jack Flaherty has been named the starter for the Tigers and will make his first start this season. The 30-year-old right-hander hasn’t pitched since last season. He last appeared on Saturday, Oct. 11, 2025 against the Seattle Mariners, when he pitched two scoreless innings out of the bullpen. Torres hit .256 last season with 22 doubles, 16 home runs and 85 walks. Riley Greene hit 36 home runs with 111 runs batted in last year. Spencer Torkelson hit .240 last season with 27 doubles, a triple, 31 home runs and 72 walks. Get more MLB picks. If you are new to sports betting, read our in-depth guide on betting on Baseball and find the best MLB betting sites and promo codes.",
